### **Formulation of Chemical Structure (Specification/Detailed Description)**

In one embodiment, the present disclosure provides a (meth)acryloyl derivative represented by the following Formula (I):

$$\left[ \text{H}_2\text{C}=\text{C}(R^{1\text{A}})-\text{C}(=\text{O})-(Z)_p \right]_m - X - (R^1)_k$$

wherein:

*   **$R^{1\text{A}}$** is independently selected at each occurrence from the group consisting of hydrogen ($-\text{H}$) and methyl ($-\text{CH}_3$);
*   **$X$** is a unsubstituted or substituted, linear, branched, or cyclic $m$-valent organic core group having from 1 to 60 carbon atoms, optionally containing one or more heteroatoms, heteroatom-containing linking groups, or repeating units designated by $(Z)_n$;
*   **$Z$** is independently selected at each occurrence from a heteroatom or a heteroatom-containing group selected from the group consisting of $-\text{O}-$, $-\text{S}-$, $-\text{NR}^a-$, $-\text{C}(=\text{O})-$, $-\text{C}(=\text{O})\text{O}-$, $-\text{OC}(=\text{O})-$, $-\text{S}(=\text{O})-$, $-\text{S}(=\text{O})_2-$, $-\text{P}(=\text{O})(R^a)-$, and $-\text{Si}(R^a)_2-$, wherein $R^a$ is hydrogen, a $C_{1}-C_{6}$ alkyl, or a $C_{6}-C_{10}$ aryl group;
*   **$R^1$** is independently selected at each occurrence from the group consisting of a substituted or unsubstituted $C_{1}-C_{20}$ alkyl group, a substituted or unsubstituted $C_{3}-C_{20}$ cycloalkyl group, and a substituted or unsubstituted $C_{6}-C_{30}$ aryl group;
*   **$m$** is an integer selected from 1 to 3;
*   **$n$** is an integer selected from 0 to 5;
*   **$k$** is an integer selected from 0 to 2; and
*   **$p$** is an integer selected from 0 to 1.

---

### **Patent Claim Drafting (Standard Independent Claim Style)**

**1. A compound of Formula (I):**

$$\left[ \text{H}_2\text{C}=\text{C}(R^{1\text{A}})-\text{C}(=\text{O})-(Z)_p \right]_m - X - (R^1)_k$$

wherein:
*   $R^{1\text{A}}$ is hydrogen or methyl;
*   $X$ is a $m$-valent organic moiety comprising from 1 to 60 carbon atoms, optionally interrupted by 0 to 5 occurrences of a heteroatom unit $(Z)_n$;
*   each $Z$ is independently selected from the group consisting of $-\text{O}-$, $-\text{S}-$, $-\text{NR}^a-$, $-\text{Si}(R^a)_2-$, and carbonyl-containing linkages, wherein $R^a$ is $H$ or $C_1-C_6$ alkyl;
*   each $R^1$ is independently selected from the group consisting of substituted or unsubstituted $C_{1}-C_{20}$ alkyl and substituted or unsubstituted $C_{6}-C_{20}$ aryl;
*   $m$ is 1, 2, or 3;
*   $n$ is 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, or 5;
*   $k$ is 0, 1, or 2; and
*   $p$ is 0 or 1.

---

### **Expanded Definitional Boilerplate (To Include in the Specification)**

> **"Organic Core Group X":** As used herein, the term " organic core group $X$" refers to a hydrocarbyl group or hetero-hydrocarbyl group having from 1 to 60 carbon atoms (e.g., 1 to 40, 1 to 20, or 2 to 10 carbon atoms). Group $X$ may be aliphatic, aromatic, or a combination thereof, and may be linear, branched, or cyclic. Group $X$ may be optionally substituted with one or more functional groups including, but not limited to, hydroxyl, halo, cyano, nitro, or alkoxy groups.
>
> **"Heteroatom Z":** As used herein, the term "heteroatom" refers to any atom other than carbon or hydrogen, preferably oxygen ($\text{O}$), nitrogen ($\text{N}$), sulfur ($\text{S}$), phosphorus ($\text{P}$), or silicon ($\text{Si}$).
>
> **"(meth)acryloyl":** The term "(meth)acryloyl" collectively refers to both acryloyl ($\text{H}_2\text{C}=\text{CH}-\text{C}(=\text{O})-$) and methacryloyl ($\text{H}_2\text{C}=\text{C}(\text{CH}_3)-\text{C}(=\text{O})-$) moieties.
